KG42.register("source_edge_archive-6fce0ce07b2ff470ab03f038",{"id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009::E::v141-c-R009-E004","paper":"07-nash_bargaining","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","rule_ref":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E004","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"settlement.payment","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E21"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C004"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-46f91650241f175b","target":"COMP-6b28b8426784699b","source_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009::V::matching.counterparties","target_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R009::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","target_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Bilateral payment entries for every distinct pair of interconnected microgrids. | Determination of P2 payments for microgrids in M′ using the optimal P1 solution. | Eligibility of interconnected microgrids for P2 payment bargaining following P1 allocation. | Identification of the active trading group M′ and allocation of its members' benefits through P2. | Payments negotiated between interconnected microgrids. | The individual-rationality restriction on each microgrid's net trading payment. | The two-stage decomposition of NBP for interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids and P2 covers the trading set M′. | The virtual clearing house's payment-clearing service for participating interconnected microgrids.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"f746d62f2753de1da781647d328770dbf9aea9d0b234b7ee68d5fe32400020b6","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Identify microgrids with nonzero beneficial P1 energy trades as the active set M-prime eligible for P2. This is trading-group membership, not pairwise offer sorting or bilateral contract bargaining.","target_definition":"Following cost-minimizing P1, active microgrids in M-prime bargain over budget-balanced bilateral payments to maximize the product of gains relative to standalone costs, subject to individual rationality. Payments need not be linear in energy; this is not a per-kWh marginal or fixed midpoint price.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Identifying the group of trading microgrids after excluding non-participants precedes allocating that group's benefits through payment bargaining. Scope: Identification of the active trading group M′ and allocation of its members' benefits through P2.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E21"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"2652","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"BP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy d- trading & scheduling and trading p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Theorem 1: The energy-trading bargaining problem NBP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy trading & scheduling and trading payment, denoted as P1 and P2, respectively. In the first step, we solve a social operating cost minimization problem P1 for the interconnected-microgrids system, which yields the optimal energy scheduling and energy trading for all microgrids. Those microgrids that trade energy with other microgrids form the set M′. In the second step, microgrids in set M′ bargain with each other to determine the energy-trading payments in P2."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":7,"printed_page":"2653","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"WANG AND HUANG: INCENTIVIZING ENERGY TRADING FOR INTERCONNECTED M microgrids do not contribute to th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"microgrids do not contribute to the social cost minimization and won't benefit from energy trading. The only criterion for determining trading and non-trading microgrids is whether they can contribute to the social cost minimization. Secondly, after identifying those microgrids who do not want to participate in the energy trading, we then focus on the rest of the microgrids who trade energy. We decide a fair allocation of benefits to each of participated microgrids through the payment bargaining problem P2."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Bilateral payment entries for every distinct pair of interconnected microgrids. | Determination of P2 payments for microgrids in M′ using the optimal P1 solution. | Eligibility of interconnected microgrids for P2 payment bargaining following P1 allocation. | Identification of the active trading group M′ and allocation of its members' benefits through P2. | Payments negotiated between interconnected microgrids. | The individual-rationality restriction on each microgrid's net trading payment. | The two-stage decomposition of NBP for interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids and P2 covers the trading set M′. | The virtual clearing house's payment-clearing service for participating interconnected microgrids.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E004","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"settlement.payment","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E21"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish the interfaces of P1 dispatch, P2 payment, the actual transaction set, and the clearing institution; the same clearing institution does not mean that the variables of P1 and P2 can be merged."}});
